   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the village of Chester\nto impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7650",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7650-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-hh-2, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7650\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the village of\nChester to impose a hotel and motel tax; and providing for the repeal of\nsuch provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation authorizes the village of Chester in Orange County to\nimpose by local law, a tax on hotel and motel occupancy of up to five\npercent of the charge.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the tax law by adding a new section 1202-hh-2, in\nrelation to the imposition of a hotel and motel tax in the Village of\nChester.\n\nSection 2: Sets effective date and repeal date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would allow the village of Chester to impose a hotel\nand motel tax. The rate of such tax shall not exceed 5W of the per diem\nrental rate for each room. Pursuant to the Municipal Home Rule Law, a\nvillage may adopt local laws that relate to the levy and administration\nof local taxes if authorized by the State legislature.  The village of\nChester has requested special legislation which will enable them to\ncollect a hotel and motel tax in an effort to raise additional revenue\nfor the village.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed 3 years after such date.\n",
